Captain Marvel is one of Marvel Comics  most aspirational figures and has  inspired a passionate fan base but when  a character has been around for this  long there are bound to be some unknown  corners at their history even for  longtime fans it's hard to find a  superhero identity that hasn't been held  by multiple people at some point from  Batman to Thor it's just part of the  territory when it comes to shaking up  the status quo so it's no surprise that  carol danvers is far from the first  person to bear the mantle of Captain  Marvel the first Captain Marvel was an  alien named Marvel a member of the Kree  species who was initially sent to earth  to observe it as a spy disguising  himself as a human scientist named  Walter Lawson he eventually took up the  identity of a superhero to protect the  very people he'd been sent to observe  but Marvel died in 1982 succumbing to  cancer as part of Marvel's first graphic  novel after the death of the first  Captain Marvel the name was passed on to  Monica Rambeau a New Orleans native who  developed a variety of powers after  being exposed to extra dimensional  energy despite having little to do with  the original Captain Marvel she spent  some time using the name as a member of  the Avengers even serving as the team's  leader at one point after Monica the  name made its way back to two of  Marvel's descendants a man named genus  Val and then a woman named phyla fell  all the while Carol Danvers was working  in the wings as Miss Marvel with an  origin story that tied her directly to  Marvel and his power set it wasn't until  2012 that she advanced to take the name  Captain Marvel for herself putting her  in the company of a rich legacy of  heroes from as far back as the earliest  days of Clark Kent it's been tricky for  superheroes to balance personal  relationships with their professional  responsibilities look at Peter Parker  whose life has constantly gone downhill  thanks to the balancing act he has to  play a Spider Man Carol Danvers  situation was even worse for a period of  time miss Marvel wasn't so much Carol  Danvers a secret identity as it was a  completely separate independent  personality after an encounter with a  Creed of ice called the psyche magnetron  fused her human DNA with the alien  Marvel she developed superpowers but at  first she wasn't consciously aware of  them  when her powers kicked in Carol blacked  out and Miss Marvel took over  it took some help from the  interdimensional being Hecate to get her  two identities under control but  whatever it took it was worth it it's  way easier to be a superhero if you can  remember what you did the next day prove  you not a scroll house crow cannot do  that while she was introduced as working  on the same Air Force Base as Marvel  Miss Marvel's solo series took her away  from the military and into the slightly  less demanding field of professional  writing she quickly lands a position as  an editor under Jay jonah Jameson The  Daily Bugle publisher who's always  giving grief to Peter Parker Carol is  brought on by Jameson as an editor of a  women's interest magazine the content of  which the two butted heads over the  cigar-chomping Jameson expected fashion  tips and housekeeping advice while  Carroll wanted to push the publication  as a progressive platform for women the  plot line established Carroll is a  character with an agenda and a  competence to pursue it her champion of  women's rights reflected the era's  ideals of empowerment and liberation  writer Kelly sue Taconic who introduced  Carroll as the new Captain Marvel in  2012 said of the debut series I'm struck  now by how overtly progressive it was  even by today's standards it took  decades for Carroll to become a captain  but she's been a superhero since the  late 70s and not always as Miss Marvel  either binary carol's second superhero  identity came about after an encounter  with rogue a power sapping member of the  x-men who temporarily stripped Carroll  of her creep hours she was later subject  to experimentation by aliens known as  the brute the results of which left her  able to get back into the superhero  action by drawing on the power of a  literal star during this period she lost  her emotional ties to earth leaving her  free to venture into outer space for new  adventures often as an ally of the x-men  by the late 90s she was angling back  toward her original skillset losing her  connection to her cosmic binary powers  and taking on the alias of war bird and  fighting as a member of the Avengers but  the loss of her binary powers brought  Carroll to a personal low at her worst  she developed a drinking habit and  became professionally unreliable with  her conduct eventually leading to her  pension from the team afterwards she  spent a few years as more of a  background character before returning to  prominence and her old name with a  second Miss Marvel Series in 2006 but as  dark as those days were for Carroll  becoming an alcoholic and getting kicked  off the Avengers is far from the worst  thing that's happened to her superhero  stories can take their characters to  some weird places but one plot turned  from Carroll's past was so twisted that  it nearly ruined her as a character it  all took place in a single-issue  1980s Avengers number 200 only three  years after Carole had made her debut as  Miss Marvel it's now widely considered  to be one of the worst comic books ever  written in the story The Avengers  discover that Miss Marvel has become  pregnant under mysterious circumstances  that in itself isn't a problem  just ask Carole's friends Spider Woman  the bizarre part is that the entire  nine-month development of her pregnancy  takes course over just a few days  resulting in a child who ages and an  impossibly fast rate the baby quickly  grows into a man named Marcus who  explains that he was previously trapped  in an alternate dimension called limbo a  world without time in which he was born  he only escaped limbo by being born  again through Miss Marvel things turned  from bizarre to frightening when Marcus  reveals that he actually kidnapped  Carole subjecting her to several weeks  worth of manipulation and mind-control  after which he impregnated her with his  essence and erased her memory of the  event to call this development creepy is  a serious understatement Tanika instead  of throwing him into the Sun Carole is  written as developing romantic feelings  for the interdimensional sex criminal  who is also her son deciding to leave  The Avengers to go back to his world  with him making things even worse  Carole's teammates don't see anything  wrong with any of it as writer and  artist Carole Strickland wrote in an  essay criticizing the issue the entire  plot is a deadly insult to every woman  fortunately for Carole's legacy the  bizarre story was effectively retcon the  next year by writer Chris Claremont who  previously wrote for the Miss Marvel  solo series Claremont took great pains  to fix the mess this story left making  it clear that Carole didn't fall in love  with her attacker but was instead  washed and when she's rescued from  Marcus's clutches  she takes the Avengers to task with  righteous fury for standing by and doing  nothing while she fell into the villains  grasp it's hard to imagine Netflix's  Jessica Jones without Trish Walker but  Trish wasn't the first character  intended to fill the supporting role the  original plans for the show included  none other than Carol Danvers as  Jessica's best friend  considering Carol's history of  intergalactic adventures her inclusion  would have made for quite a different  show or at least a very stripped-down  version of Carol  now that Netflix's Marvel partnership  has come to an end it's probably for the  best that Carol stayed on the film side  of the equation after all Captain Marvel  once fought off an entire fleet of  spaceships single-handedly and that's  the kind of thing that begs to be seen  in a movie  her powers are big budgets once that  Hawkeye ever do that compares to that  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorites topper coming soon  subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

